Package: s3bibliometric
Type: Package
Title: Semantic Similarity Score (S3) for Mapping Research Fields
Version: 0.14.5
Authors@R: c(
    person("Hamid", "Bekamiri", email = "hamidb@business.aau.dk",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Christian Richter", "Østergaard", role = "ctb",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-1782-202X", note = "S3 method co-author")),
    person("Bram", "Timmermans", role = "ctb",
           comment = c(note = "S3 method co-author")))
Description: Maps the intellectual structure of a research field from the
    titles and abstracts of its papers with the Semantic Similarity Score (S3)
    method (Bekamiri, Østergaard and Timmermans, 2027,
    <doi:10.1016/j.jbusres.2026.116582>): transformer embeddings, a
    time-ordered similarity graph and Leiden community detection, with
    citation-based indicators of the communities. The package is an R
    interface to the 's3-bibliometric' Python library, so R and Python give
    the same results: run the analysis, read communities and answers as data
    frames, compare text-only and hybrid maps, and write a report organised
    for a literature review.
